{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>תענה</b> — two times: אם ענה תענה, אם תענה את בנותי. This is what they expounded: אם תענה — from marital relations, as we learn from here, for it is written אלמנה ויתום לא תענון and adjacent to it אם ענה תענה — that one must not afflict them in the manner of widowhood, i.e., must not leave them bundles like a living widow. לא תענון — nun of plural; אם ענה תענה — singular: one affliction is multiplied and one affliction is slight. Another interpretation: to teach that all Israel are guarantors for one another, so that even if one afflicts, it is as though all afflicted. ענה תענה · צעק יצעק · שמע אשמע — all are doubled, to say: all by the measure you do to him, I do to you."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:05.214361594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}